---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import LangBanner from '../LangBanner.astro';
import { dict } from '../../lib/i18n.mjs';
interface Props { lang: string }
const { lang } = Astro.props;
const t = dict(lang);
---
<Base title={t.contribute.title} lang={lang} description={t.contribute.description}>
  <p class="eyebrow">{t.contribute.eyebrow}</p>
  <h1>{t.contribute.title}</h1>
  <LangBanner lang={lang} kind="enOnly" />
  <div lang="en">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>The draft improves the way open source improves: in public, by
    pull request, against stated criteria. Three repositories:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/ownthemachine/own-the-machine">own-the-machine</a>:
      the law, its memorandum, the review ledger (CC BY-SA 4.0).</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/ownthemachine/own-the-machine-tools">own-the-machine-tools</a>:
      the review gates and linter (MIT).</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/ownthemachine/own-the-machine-site">own-the-machine-site</a>:
      this site (AGPL-3.0).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The merge criteria</h2>
    <p>Every change to the legal text must survive four tests: it claims
    assets, not flows; it reaches every citizen equally; it is
    raid-proof; and it claims the stake in time, at the moment gains
    crystallise. Mechanical constraints (the DC table in the
    <a href="/law/objections">objections</a>) and six adversarial review
    gates apply before merge. A pull request that weakens a protection
    needs to say so in plain language.</p>

    <h2>Ways in</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Argue.</strong> Take on an objection, or raise a new
      one at full strength. The strongest contribution is the attack we
      have not answered.</li>
      <li><strong>Draft.</strong> Improve an article against the Joint
      Practical Guide conventions; the linter and gates will meet you.</li>
      <li><strong>Translate.</strong> Languages are promoted from
      machine-translated to human-verified one page at a time; native
      readers are the bottleneck.</li>
      <li><strong>Build.</strong> The site and tools are ordinary open
      source with issues waiting.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 { font-size: 1.7rem; margin: 0.4rem 0 1.2rem; }
</style>
